## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates offline-first routing with on-device compute, real-time edge-weight updates, crash safety, and cryptographic authenticity. It also tests SwiftUI/Combine integration and mobile performance optimization.

## Key Concepts
- **Graph algorithms**: A* with incremental weight updates
- **Offline-first data store**: SQLite with write-ahead logging for durability
- **Streaming ingestion**: Combine for processing traffic events
- **Crash safety**: Checkpoints and state persistence for reliable resume
- **Cryptographic verification**: CryptoKit for signed map updates
- **SwiftUI dashboard**: Route visualization with ETA and confidence metrics

## Code Example
```swift
// Graph structure
struct Node: Hashable { let id: String; let coordinate: CLLocationCoordinate2D }
struct Edge { let from: Node.ID; let to: Node.ID; var weight: Double }

class RoutingEngine: ObservableObject {
    @Published var currentRoute: [Node] = []
    @Published var eta: TimeInterval = 0
    @Published var confidence: Double = 0

    private var graph: AdjacencyList<Node.ID, Edge>
    private var checkpoint: RouteCheckpoint?

    // MARK: - A* with Checkpoint Resume
    func computeRoute(from start: Node.ID, to end: Node.ID) {
        let checkpoint = RouteCheckpoint(currentNode: start)
        currentRoute = aStar(graph: graph, start: start, goal: end, checkpoint: checkpoint)
        self.checkpoint = checkpoint
        updateETA()
    }

    func invalidateEdges(_ edges: [Edge.ID]) {
        guard let cp = checkpoint else { return }
        currentRoute = aStar(graph: graph, start: cp.currentNode, goal: goal, checkpoint: cp)
        updateConfidence()
    }

    // MARK: - Combine Traffic Ingestion
    private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()

    func subscribe(to publisher: AnyPublisher<TrafficEvent, Never>) {
        publisher
            .filter { $0.isSignificant }
            .sink { [weak self] event in
                self?.applyTrafficEvent(event)
            }
            .store(in: &cancellables)
    }

    private func applyTrafficEvent(_ event: TrafficEvent) {
        graph.updateWeight(edgeId: event.edgeId, weight: event.delay)
        invalidateEdges([event.edgeId])
    }

    // MARK: - Map Update Verification
    func verifyAndApplyMapUpdate(_ update: MapUpdate) throws {
        try CryptoKit.verify(update.signature, for: update.data)
        try applyMapUpdate(update)
        checkpoint = nil // Invalidate checkpoint after structural changes
    }
}
```

## Test Plan

| Category | Test Case | Method |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| Routing | A* finds optimal path on static graph | XCTest with known graph |
| Routing | Returns to checkpoint on weight update | Mock weight change, verify partial recomputation |
| Streaming | Traffic events update weights correctly | Combine test publisher, assert graph state |
| Offline | Route computed without network | Disable network, run computeRoute |
| Crash Safety | Resume from checkpoint after simulated crash | Inject crash state, verify recovery |
| Crypto | Reject tampered map updates | Modify signature, expect CryptoKit error |
| UI | Dashboard reflects route/ETA/confidence | ViewInspector snapshot tests |

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses secure offline-first data vault design, practical crypto in Swift, and testability across device loss and passphrase changes.

## Key Concepts
- CryptoKit: AES-GCM, HKDF-SHA256
- KDF with per-note salt; envelope key in Secure Enclave
- CoreData for local metadata; CloudKit for encrypted blob sync
- Key rotation and re-wrapping strategies
- Testing: offline scenarios, passphrase rotation, data integrity

## Code Example
```swift
import CryptoKit

func deriveKey(password: String, salt: Data) -> SymmetricKey {
  let ikm = SymmetricKey(data: Data(password.utf8))
  let key = HKDF<SHA256>.deriveKey(inputKeyMaterial: ikm, salt: salt, info: Data(), outputByteCount: 32)
  return key
}
```

```swift
// Encryption
func encrypt(plaintext: Data, key: SymmetricKey) throws -> Data {
  let sealed = try AES.GCM.seal(plaintext, using: key)
  return sealed.combined!
}
```

```swift
// Decryption
func decrypt(data: Data, key: SymmetricKey) throws -> Data {
  let box = try AES.GCM.SealedBox(combined: data)
  return try AES.GCM.open(box, using: key)
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical local persistence, SwiftUI queries, and basic user experience actions without requiring remote data.

## Key Concepts
- Codable persistence to the local Documents directory
- File-based store with load/save and proper error handling
- SwiftUI List with searchable and dynamic filtering by multiple fields
- Row actions: copy to clipboard and share sheet
- Basic test plan and empty-state handling

## Code Example
```swift
struct Snippet: Codable, Identifiable {
    let id: UUID
    var title: String
    var content: String
    var tag: String
    var createdDate: Date
}

class SnippetStore: ObservableObject {
    @Published var snippets: [Snippet] = []

    private let fileName = "snippets.json"

    private var fileURL: URL {
        FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask)[0]
            .appendingPathComponent(fileName)
    }

    func load() {
        guard FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: fileURL.path) else { return }
        do {
            let data = try Data(contentsOf: fileURL)
            snippets = try JSONDecoder().decode([Snippet].self, from: data)
        } catch {
            print("Failed to load: \(error)")
        }
    }

    func save() {
        do {
            let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(snippets)
            try data.write(to: fileURL)
        } catch {
            print("Failed to save: \(error)")
        }
    }
}

struct ContentView: View {
    @StateObject private var store = SnippetStore()
    @State private var searchText = ""

    var filteredSnippets: [Snippet] {
        if searchText.isEmpty { return store.snippets }
        let query = searchText.lowercased()
        return store.snippets.filter {
            $0.title.lowercased().contains(query) ||
            $0.content.lowercased().contains(query) ||
            $0.tag.lowercased().contains(query)
        }
    }

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            Group {
                if store.snippets.isEmpty {
                    ContentUnavailableView(
                        "No Snippets",
                        systemImage: "doc.text",
                        description: Text("Add your first snippet to get started")
                    )
                } else {
                    List(filteredSnippets) { snippet in
                        VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                            Text(snippet.title).font(.headline)
                            Text(snippet.content).lineLimit(2).foregroundStyle(.secondary)
                            Text(snippet.tag).font(.caption).padding(4).background(Color.blue.opacity(0.2)).cornerRadius(4)
                        }
                        .contextMenu {
                            Button("Copy") {
                                UIPasteboard.general.string = snippet.content
                            }
                            ShareLink(item: snippet.content)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            .navigationTitle("SnippetBook")
            .searchable(text: $searchText, prompt: "Search snippets")
            .onAppear { store.load() }
        }
    }
}
```

## Test Plan
1. **Persistence Test**: Launch app, add snippets, kill app, relaunch — snippets should persist
2. **Search Test**: Type in search field — results should filter by title, content, or tag
3. **Empty State Test**: Launch fresh — empty state should display
4. **Actions Test**: Long-press row — copy and share options should work

